# Same line endings on every OS: LF everywhere (bash needs it for run_all.sh, and suite_tests_sha hashes
# tests.csv and the kernels byte for byte), except Windows batch files, which need CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.ipynb text eol=lf
# Result files are kept byte for byte as each program wrote them (Python's csv module and R on Windows write CRLF).
results/** -text
